# Check every text file out with LF line endings on all platforms (GitHub's
# Windows runners set core.autocrlf=true, which would otherwise give CRLF
# working trees). The insta snapshots depend on byte-identical .cairo
# fixtures: the Cairo compiler names generated inner functions (loops,
# closures) with byte-offset spans — e.g. `bad_loop[136-339]` — and CRLF
# line endings shift every offset, changing the SIERRA function names that
# detector messages embed.
* text=auto eol=lf
